# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Several tests read source and documentation as text and match against it: `docstatus.test.ts`
# scans headings, `safewrite.test.ts` scans imports, `web.test.ts` scans stylesheets and markup.
# **A regex that anchors with `$` behaves differently under CRLF** — `.` does not match a line
# terminator in JavaScript and `\r` is one — so `(.*)$` matches nothing at all on a Windows
# checkout. `docstatus.test.ts` shipped with exactly that bug: green on the author's tree, red on a
# fresh clone, and reporting conflicts that were not there.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than plain `text=auto`, because `text=auto` still hands Windows a CRLF working
# tree and the tests read the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text, whatever a heuristic decides.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.syx binary
*.dnprj binary
*.dn2prj binary
